            "review_text": "jnodar\nCamden, Australia113 contributions\n0\nYummy\nNov 2018\nBánh Khọt Cô Ba Vũng Tàu is a fantastic restaurant in Ho Chi Mein City (HCM City).\n\nWe were welcomed and delighted with the small misting spray that refreshed us as we walked into this establishment. \n\nOur meal consisted of two mains (the large Vietnamese pancake – (Ba’nh Xe’o Co’ba and the mini pancake Ba’nh knot Co’ba ). The Ba’nh Xe’o Co’ba is a large pancake with pork and shrimp and the Ba’nh knot Co’ba is a mini pancake with shrimp and you dunk them in a sweet sauce (I added chili to mine also) and both were delicious, but we enjoyed the mini pancakes more. \n\nChilled coconut juice also had a pleasant hit to our palates. There were more items to savour but we just could not eat any more. \n\nWe recommended you try this establishment next time you visit HCM City\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 27, 2018",
