            "review_text": "Quoc T\n10 contributions\n0\nA Forever Summer Taste of Vietnamese Crepes\nMay 2018 • Family\nPlease note that there are several locations having the same name: You would want to make sure to go to this particular location. You won't regret it. The food is fabulous and the price is so reasonable I often feel guilty paying so little for so much food...\n\nFavorite dishes: Spring rolls, fried egg rolls, crepe with prawns, crepe with ground pork, banh xeo, fried rice w shrimps, etc. The fresh vegetables are fresh and absolutely safe to consume. \n\nOrder TWO cold drinks per person right from the start--since the heat will engulf you immediately upon sitting down, and having TWO cold beers in hand would be most welcome. Another drink you would want to try is the fresh coconuts that are served cold in their thick husky cover. The juice is elegantly sweet and do not forget to ask for a spoon to scoop out the flesh to enjoy after finishing drinking it.\n\nAhh, Ho Chi Minh City and its iconic restaurants!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten August 27, 2018",
