            "review_text": "InkosiAU\nSydney, Australia171 contributions\n0\nNice place, don’t believe Google Maps for correct location\nDec 2017\nOur hotel recommended we eat here tonight, as we wanted to experience what the locals eat. We jumped in an Uber, but both Uber and Google Maps have the location wrong. It’s on the right street, but at the opposite end of where both Uber and Google think it is. We eventually found it, after asking about 10 locals who had no idea what we were taking about. \n\nMost of the food was nice -the beef stir fry was especially good, as were the spring rolls. There must have been a communication break down as we also ordered a pancake with beef but got one with prawns and squid instead - no one was a fan of it. Prawns still had their shells on, and didn’t seem that fresh. (We do live on the Sunshine Coast in Australia where we eat prawns that are caught fresh each day and of exceptional quality - so we are spoilt in this regard)\n\nService was friendly - nothing over the top, but it was good. \n\nAnd cheap!! 4 of us ate for AUD$22. Pretty amazing.\nRead more\nWritten December 29, 2017",
